# Agent worktrees — checkouts of this repo, nested inside it. Not content, and
# an unignored one shows up as untracked in every `git status`. The sibling
# repos ignore this for a sharper reason: there a release script reads
# `git status --porcelain` and refuses to publish a "dirty" tree, so a stray
# worktree blocks a release (flipbase/recorder#267). This repo has no such
# check — here it is only noise — but the entry belongs in all of them.
.claude/worktrees/
